import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"mlopt-kit — the modular handl composition, proven end to end","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"mlopt-kit — the modular handl composition, proven end to end","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/mlopt-kit.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/mlopt-kit.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/mlopt-kit.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="mlopt-kit-—-the-modular-handl-composition-proven-end-to-end" tabindex="-1">mlopt-kit — the modular handl composition, proven end to end <a class="header-anchor" href="#mlopt-kit-—-the-modular-handl-composition-proven-end-to-end" aria-label="Permalink to “mlopt-kit — the modular handl composition, proven end to end”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date:</strong> 2026-10-19 · <strong>Surface:</strong> <code>packages/mlopt-kit/</code> (new Rust crate, root cargo workspace) · <strong>Gate:</strong> <code>cargo test -p mlopt-kit</code> — <strong>16/16 green</strong>.</p><h2 id="what-landed" tabindex="-1">What landed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-landed" aria-label="Permalink to “What landed”">​</a></h2><p><code>mlopt-kit</code> is mlopt&#39;s seam to the modular handl stack — a plain Rust library crate (the <code>mlopt-native</code> layout precedent: no PyO3, no Python changes beyond a uv-workspace exclude line). It assembles the smallest honest runtime for mlopt&#39;s use:</p><ul><li><strong>Language</strong> — <code>handl_kit_data_canonical::language_from_yaml()</code> (the canonical <code>Language</code> as data), installed process-wide via <code>plugin-lib-handl::install_default_language</code> so lazily-built <code>.hnl</code> module bridge runtimes bind it (ADR-0128 §&quot;the 0.8 seam&quot;).</li><li><strong>Engines</strong> — the three the canonical kit defaults to: <code>data</code> lex (<code>DataLexerEngine</code>), <code>pratt</code> parse (<code>PrattEngine</code>), <code>tree-walk</code> eval (<code>TreeWalkEngine</code>). No sdkgen/compile/lint/lsp. Engine selection is by name through <code>EngineRegistry</code>/<code>RuntimeConfig</code>; <code>CatoptKit::new_with_registry</code> is the injection seam for more later.</li><li><strong>Modules</strong> — <code>host-tensor</code>&#39;s <code>TENSOR_HNL</code> interface as a <code>HandlModule</code> over <code>tensor_op_registry()</code> (all 18 <code>tensor.*</code> ops), in a <code>ModuleRegistry</code> layered under <code>handl_runtime::fp</code>&#39;s <code>field_access</code>/<code>fanout</code> host fns. <code>field_access</code> makes <code>tensor.matmul(a,b)</code> dispatch with no injected globals: unbound <code>tensor</code> → <code>&quot;tensor&quot;</code> → <code>&quot;tensor.matmul&quot;</code> → <code>ModuleLookup</code> → <code>OpFunction</code>.</li><li><strong>Imports</strong> — a <code>ModuleLoader</code> is wired into the eval engine (and into the loader&#39;s own engine for nested imports), so <code>import &quot;./f.hnl&quot;</code> works relative to <code>module_root</code>, and <code>CatoptKit::new_with_project</code> reads <code>.handl.toml</code> <code>[dependencies]</code> via <code>handl_platform::resolve_dependencies</code>.</li><li><strong><code>run_tagged</code></strong> — a second wired engine kept for the <code>TaggedValue</code>-returning eval path (<code>eval_tagged</code>), so a tensor op result can be observed as the real <code>TaggedValue::Tensor</code> variant with no <code>serde_json::Value</code> round-trip.</li></ul><p>Deps float on <code>main</code> as git deps (kernel/lang/platform/host-tensor); the local-override story is <code>~/.cache/devin/handl_deps.env</code> (git insteadOf → <code>~/GitHub/handl-lang/*</code> checkouts) with the handl-lang <code>[patch]</code> convention documented in the root <code>Cargo.toml</code>.</p><h2 id="verified-end-to-end-tests-compose-rs" tabindex="-1">Verified end to end (<code>tests/compose.rs</code>) <a class="header-anchor" href="#verified-end-to-end-tests-compose-rs" aria-label="Permalink to “Verified end to end (tests/compose.rs)”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>tensor.to_list(tensor.matmul(from_list([[1,2],[3,4]]), from_list([[5,6],[7,8]])))</code> → <code>[[19,22],[43,50]]</code> through the assembled runtime — real <code>.hnl</code> → real tensor work.</li><li><code>run</code> returns the <code>{&quot;__tensor__&quot;:…}</code> wire form; <code>TaggedValue::from</code> decodes it to <code>TaggedValue::Tensor</code> (<code>shape [2,2]</code>, <code>data [19,22,43,50]</code>); <code>run_tagged</code> returns the <strong>Tensor variant directly</strong> — never an <code>Obj</code> fallback.</li><li>Chained ops inside one program (<code>add(matmul(a,b), ones)</code>) — the tensor round-trips through the <code>Function</code> boundary each hop.</li><li>conv2d (1×1 NCHW) and batch_norm (eval mode, <code>eps=0</code>) smokes — both match <code>host-tensor</code>&#39;s own spec values.</li><li><code>tensor.derive(&quot;batch_norm&quot;)</code> → <code>&quot;tensor.batch_norm_backward&quot;</code>; unpaired → <code>null</code> — the optimization-loop surface.</li><li><strong><code>.handl.toml</code> name resolution works</strong>: a temp project with <code>host-tensor = { path = &quot;host-tensor&quot; }</code> (the embedded <code>TENSOR_HNL</code> vendored as <code>index.hnl</code>) supports both <code>from &quot;host-tensor&quot; import tensor</code> and <code>import * as t</code>.</li><li>A consumer-authored <code>.hnl</code> module (<code>linalg.hnl</code> with a <code>from &quot;host-tensor&quot; import tensor</code> header and an <code>export double_matmul</code> arrow) imports and runs — the shape a mlopt-side <code>.hnl</code> module would take.</li></ul><h2 id="named-gap-—-closed-2026-10-19-second-pass" tabindex="-1">Named gap — closed (2026-10-19, second pass) <a class="header-anchor" href="#named-gap-—-closed-2026-10-19-second-pass" aria-label="Permalink to “Named gap — closed (2026-10-19, second pass)”">​</a></h2><p>A <em>checked-in</em> <code>.handl.toml</code> can now name the <code>host-tensor</code> dep <strong>portably</strong>: platform <code>90853ec2</code> added the git-package→dir bridge — <code>[dependencies]</code> entries accept <code>{ git = …, rev|branch|tag }</code> and a <code>[patch]</code> table is the consumer-side local override (the Cargo <code>[patch]</code>/dev-link story: a patch whose directory exists wins, a missing one is inert). <code>packages/mlopt-kit/.handl.toml</code> declares <code>host-tensor = { git = &quot;https://github.com/handl-lang/host-tensor&quot;, branch = &quot;main&quot; }</code> + <code>[patch]</code> → the sibling checkout&#39;s <code>src/</code> (the dir holding <code>index.hnl</code>); an unpatched git dep resolves to its <code>~/.handl/pkg/&lt;name&gt;</code> cache slot — the dir the ADR-0010 fetch hook will populate (a symlink there is today&#39;s stand-in). Both resolution arms are asserted in <code>tests/conv_bn.rs</code>.</p><h2 id="the-shipped-consumer-—-hnl-conv-bn-hnl-the-conv-bn-fold-end-to-end" tabindex="-1">The shipped consumer — <code>hnl/conv_bn.hnl</code>, the conv+BN fold end to end <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-shipped-consumer-—-hnl-conv-bn-hnl-the-conv-bn-fold-end-to-end" aria-label="Permalink to “The shipped consumer — hnl/conv_bn.hnl, the conv+BN fold end to end”">​</a></h2><p>The crate now ships the <code>.hnl</code> program mlopt&#39;s e-graph optimizes: <code>conv_bn</code> is the unfolded <code>batch_norm(conv2d(x, W, b), γ, β, μ, σ²)</code> composite — the <code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code>/<code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> fold site — and <code>conv_bn_fold</code> is the minted rewrite&#39;s RHS evaluated: <code>s = γ·rsqrt(σ²+ε)</code> per channel (the op surface has no elementwise pow, so <code>channel_scales</code> is a <code>while</code>-loop over the materialized stat lists using scalar <code>**</code>), <code>W′ = W∘reshape(s, (C,1,1,1))</code>, <code>b′ = b∘s + (β − s∘μ)</code>, then a single <code>conv2d</code>. <code>bn_adjoint</code>/<code>bn_grad</code> compose <code>tensor.derive</code>/<code>batch_norm_backward</code> — the registered-adjoint surface. <code>tests/conv_bn.rs</code> proves <code>TaggedValue::Tensor</code> results and <em>exact</em> folded-vs-unfolded agreement on a dyadic fixture (conv out <code>[[12,15],[6,5]]</code> → BN/folded <code>[[37,46],[4,3]]</code>; dx/dγ/dβ <code>[3,3,1,1]</code>/<code>[27,2.5]</code>/<code>[2,2]</code>). The consumer story the fold&#39;s premise-pay measurement (<code>fold-cost-single-source.md</code>) pointed at: the same program the e-graph folds is the program the kit runs.</p><h2 id="one-environment-note" tabindex="-1">One environment note <a class="header-anchor" href="#one-environment-note" aria-label="Permalink to “One environment note”">​</a></h2><p>The tree-walk engine recurses deeply enough on ordinary expressions to overflow libtest&#39;s 2 MiB default test-thread stack (<code>conv2d</code>&#39;s 4-deep literals hit it). Both upstream suites carry the same knob — repo-root <code>.cargo/config.toml</code> sets <code>RUST_MIN_STACK = 32 MiB</code>, matching <code>kit-canonical/.cargo/config.toml</code>. Not a composition blocker — an upstream-documented constraint.</p><h2 id="what-this-is-not-yet" tabindex="-1">What this is not (yet) <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-is-not-yet" aria-label="Permalink to “What this is not (yet)”">​</a></h2><p>No Python surface (that is <code>mlopt-native</code>&#39;s maturin shape when needed); no <code>bytecode</code>/typecheck/compile engines registered (the registry seam admits them by name); no package <em>fetch</em> — an unpatched git dep resolves to its <code>~/.handl/pkg</code> slot, which nothing populates yet (the ADR-0010 fetch hook is upstream&#39;s follow-up; a checkout/symlink there is the stand-in). The e-graph itself still lives Python-side — the kit runs the folded <em>program</em>; lowering mlopt IR to <code>.hnl</code> is the direction the seam opens, not something this crate does.</p>`,16)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};